# android.hardware.graphics.composer@2.1-service — device extras.

# Display hotplug / vsync uevent listener.
#
# FACT (live device, 2026-08-10):
#   avc: denied { read } for comm="UEventThreadHWC"
#        scontext=u:r:hal_graphics_composer_default:s0
#        tcontext=u:r:hal_graphics_composer_default:s0
#        tclass=netlink_kobject_uevent_socket  permissive=1           (x28)
#
# The thread name is the giveaway: this is SurfaceFlinger's HWC uevent thread
# inside the composer process, sitting on the kernel uevent netlink socket
# waiting for display change/hotplug notifications.
#
# AOSP does not cover it: system/sepolicy/public/hal_graphics_composer.te has
# no netlink_kobject_uevent_socket rule at all (grepped). Only `read` was
# denied, so create/bind are evidently already reachable, but the whole set is
# granted here because a listener that can create and bind but not read is a
# state no caller can recover from, and the four permissions are meaningless
# apart.
#
# Without it, under enforcing: the composer opens the socket and then blocks
# forever on a read it is not allowed to make. Display hotplug and any
# HWC-driven mode change stop being noticed. On a fixed-panel phone that is
# survivable day to day, which is exactly why it would go unnoticed - it
# surfaces as SurfaceFlinger missing a state change it should have seen.
allow hal_graphics_composer_default self:netlink_kobject_uevent_socket { create bind read setopt };
